" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d34f2bd-1406-50c4-9338-867f1ecca34e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213405" :question/problem "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36?$\n- **I.** $5$\n- **II.** $13$\n- **III.** $24$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $5$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(5,36)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $13$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(13,36)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $24$ does *not* have a multiplicative inverse modulo $36$ since $\\text{gcd}(24,36)=12\\ne 1.\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04206f72-e018-5925-a58f-179e897595dc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Existence of a Multiplicative Inverse" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050670 :topic/id #uuid "5da1bf0d-a741-59f5-981a-d9099d93b347" :topic/math-academy-id 4818 :topic/title "Multiplicative Inverses Modulo N"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c0cc1a3-a6c9-58b2-b8d1-fdb7cfba42c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472940} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e8c3d3-362b-5f70-8fb3-4119be1b3ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e8c3d3-362b-5f70-8fb3-4119be1b3ca1" :answer/type {:db