tion.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af0eb712-6f36-542d-b37c-e07c5fedf4a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-213407" :question/problem "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27?$\n- **I.** $11$\n- **II.** $16$\n- **III.** $23$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $11$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(11,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $16$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(16,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $23$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(23,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65e9c4fd-dae7-5858-b008-ca0e144fa64a" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Binary Relations Using Digraphs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048710 :topic/id #uuid "b73e30a4-d62d-555b-a6f7-1a03dfa6cf83" :topic/math-academy-id 4837 :topic/title "Graphical Representations of Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08d4af0-3773-548f-9fff-8a490f817fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472916} {:answer/id #uuid "59490e6a-5908-57a3-8fef-747cf7e201bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59490e6a-5908-57a3-8fef-747cf7e201bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472917} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f20679a-5582-56e8-8163-a7d88ca1181c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203fb9b8-f545-5d2f-89ff-f4983703dc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472918} {:answer/id #uuid "59cd232f-66c8-56d0-9097-b8c0d32be4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203fb9b8-f545-5d2f-89ff-f4983703dc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472918} :answer-field/id #uuid "91133de6-9099-5c69-a30a-e54e18188597" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa1d7eb8-65e2-508b-bd06-79c281dcc46b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472920} {:answer/id #uuid "b489d262-5a96-5a75-a605-5ac9116d6ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b489d262-5a96-5a75-a605-5ac9116d6ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472921} :answer-field/id #uuid "d300fddb-6ab1-5e91-97cd-d78d9057470d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "538c45af-5de6-56ca-85b6-7f902af26d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-213261" :question/problem "![](images/de/ded4e8a94730585809c5534fee8d401481c919d529a67cd088e96b8797f2b237.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set $\\{2,5,8\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(2,8)$\n\nIII. $(8,5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation can be visualized using a directed graph (digraph), where \n\n- the nodes (vertices) of the graph are elements of the underlying set,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines an arrow from node $x$ to node $y$,\n\n- each pair $(x,x)$ from the relation defines a loop from node $x$ to itself.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(2,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has a loop from the node $2$ to itself.\n\n- The pair $(2,8)$ does not belong to the relation since the directed graph does not have an arrow that starts at the node $2$ and ends at the node $8.$\n\n- The pair $(8,5)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has an arrow that starts at the node $8$ and ends at the node $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65e9c4fd-dae7-5858-b008-ca0e144fa64a" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Binary Relations Using Digraphs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048710 :topic/id #uuid "b73e30a4-d62d-555b-a6f7-1a03dfa6cf83" :topic/math-academy-id 4837 :topic/title "Graphical Representations of Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76eb6889-3903-5edc-98cf-ffd76ae6f40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472922} {:answer/id #uuid "0324bb18-7e2f-576d-80aa-e4ccc4597d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76eb6889-3903-5edc-98cf-ffd76ae6f40c" :an