ion of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expressions I and II are statistics. They are functions of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{9}$ only.\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu $ and the unknown population standard deviation $\\sigma .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049367 :topic/id #uuid "ef34739b-f46e-5073-bcb9-1acc5022fae9" :topic/math-academy-id 3864 :topic/title "Sampling Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0578fb-717b-50d7-a9ba-f9b58027da4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472694} {:answer/id #uuid "e0971c4c-4b9f-5717-82e8-622a06065584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c0578fb-717b-50d7-a9ba-f9b58027da4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472694} :answer-field/id #uuid "8045efcc-7dd9-5c24-bcee-feebb8da7476" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1251003-cc51-5f92-82cf-e0c639820199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472696} {:answer/id #uuid "18bff3ee-6f28-5bfc-bb1d-a5240b9ab377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db