es representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression I is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression II is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{6}$ only.\n\n- Expression III is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{6}$ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049367 :topic/id #uuid "ef34739b-f46e-5073-bcb9-1acc5022fae9" :topic/math-academy-id 3864 :topic/title "Sampling Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382fcb4b-1f5a-5e40-9b1a-48b7ea9c1908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472706} {:answer/id #uuid "193e4ff8-497e-534d-a890-32a515d03a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "193e4ff8-497e-534d-a890-32a515d03a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472707} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd9a7cf-5f28-57f4-b962-ba73cdc48d2c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e0fe096-cbd6-530f-94bb-de2910c9a7a8" :ans