w a Poisson distribution. The average points scored on the math test is not an event that occurs at a constant average rate.\n\n- Random variable II follows a Poisson distribution. The number of orders can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a month).\n\n- Random variable III follows a Poisson distribution. Again, the number of calls can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a week).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048934 :topic/id #uuid "cd3b7077-78e5-5eb6-880e-d8648790c6b0" :topic/math-academy-id 2838 :topic/title "Modeling With the Poisson Distribution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a83b8bf-f148-5771-ab62-abc8a88c89c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473470} {:answer/id #uuid "200b2717-b678-52c8-a38b-dcc7faf7cd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "200b2717-b678-52c8-a38b-dcc7faf7cd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473471} :answer-field/id #uuid "e23d02e7-d019-5ab2-b8a2-218471927da5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0957a551-1026-56a8-b1ca-b6ab46d9b0e8" :answer/type