:answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2486be8-75b8-51f1-882e-08f8a79961f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42463" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **II.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ca319c5-9f62-51e3-b670-611fc8a8daaa" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Critical Point Using the Second Partial Derivatives Test" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051048 :topic/id #uuid "7d157e41-c50b-570b-8b5b-b8a5a0d03163" :topic/math-academy-id 1944 :topic/title "The Second Partial Derivatives Test"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f54eb3dc-8f1a-5dd1-962f-c6bca73b03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477271} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3bd524-ddd5-53ed-ac7b-67c5c3c6cc25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54eb3dc-8f1a-5dd1-962f-c6bca73b03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477271} :answer-field/id #uuid "665a7adb-4995-5ab8-8dc0-620e006ab150" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32a85eda-3d96-59fb-ae1a-38073082f1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477273} {:answer/id #uuid "dc13ebbc-79a8-5f41-b29b-888f990acc60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc13ebbc-79a8-5f41-b29b-888f990acc60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477274} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e1f0653-0d7e-5971-b6ae-0758b0a5f1c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e834f58-d2a9-5c2a-898e-e22835894832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477275} {:answer/id #uuid "793854ab-f508-5b37-924d-9eca03e5429b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e834f58-d2a9-5c2a-898e-e22835894832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477275} :answer-field/id #uuid "56acc568-b4e3-5dd3-8613-65932ac1d099" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477607}] :question/id #uuid "d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37456" :question/problem "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(1,1)>0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det({f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=({f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420497} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420523} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545198} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545989}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fbefaa-38d7-5b1f-be3b-d344a924b231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474672} {:answer/id #uuid "3aff4692-6312-58ed-98f2-0a3443f6028f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2fbefaa-38d7-5b1f-be3b-d344a924b231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474672} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7c98675-6c8c-5b6c-81a1-9c741a4b1fef" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ce5643-56db-5b30-bf6c-3f04636fd51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474674} {:answer/id #uuid "c65cb16b-cf7f-5925-b88c-a3e129bea8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c65cb16b-cf7f-5925-b88c-a3e129bea8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474675} :answer-field/id #uuid "20daba64-8669-59a5-ac11-cb70500da589" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "617bd55d-af8f-5b9b-b339-9b8aba87ef0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474676} {:answer/id #uuid "02316f99-71bd-5da0-a01a-6cebde20bdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "617bd55d-af8f-5b9b-b339-9b8aba87ef0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474676} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8022e07-677e-5054-a8ba-974ea9f7d635" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00b6d002-6ca8-5b5f-a710-55bc4f02fb94" :question/math-academy-id "q-216443" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n\\ge -4$\n- **II.** $n=-4$\n- **III.** $|n|\\le 4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solutions to the given equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+7n+12 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n+3) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n\\ge -4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $n\\ge -4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=-4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=-4,$ then ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|\\le 4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $|n|\\le 4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c974654-2cb6-5b5b-97a1-e7952338aa19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474514} {:answer/id #uuid "77ac130e-f100-51be-bd73-406df515704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c974654-2cb6-5b5b-97a1-e7952338aa19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474514} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c88976d-d907-52f4-b47a-d7b43494e038" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b124e103-45ef-5879-b034-67056b95ce39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474516} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb1842c-fdd9-5de9-8f9c-62da69dba519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b124e103-45ef-5879-b034-67056b95ce39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474516} :answer-field/id #uuid "0feb969b-f2b9-5a1a-83bd-b7a42fa61e97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66d71eb4-f061-5c7b-9f2d-10d55ca0c471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474518} {:answer/id #uuid "51e51cb2-94cf-54a5-bbf1-cbeee409ec60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e51cb2-94cf-54a5-bbf1-cbeee409ec60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474519} :answer-field/id #uuid "129babf3-fc18-5e17-9e10-6f9c8b2b5687" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04618c03-3ca0-590d-b082-33d1176f03c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-172300" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an even number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n$ is an odd number\n- **II.** $n$ is a positive number\n- **III.** $n$ is a multiple of $2$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number })\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is an odd number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=2$ is not an odd number but ${2}^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇏\\,(\\text{ is a positive number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=-2$ is not a positive number, but $(-2)^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is even, it must also be true that $n$ is even. Therefore, $n$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b