-6c36718e49e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc96775f-c6f5-5ca4-9703-f26d24ae7c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1764754-6220-5bd9-aaab-c9961114c472" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10fd92b2-5e05-5850-b7d2-d8140b9fd04f" :question/math-academy-id "q-172315" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}=16$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n=4$\n- **II.** $-4<n<4$\n- **III.** $|n|<16$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n-4) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=4,$ then ${n}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(-4<n<4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1\\ne 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<16)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<16,$ but ${n}^{2}=1\\ne 16.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6918f073-c442-5f18-b455-52622f56f35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474538} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf41748-06d6-52c6-aa3b-308d83a706dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6918f073-c442-5f18-b455-52622f56f35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474538} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d8263b8-7e82-5b77-9f03-bec084e88fd5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9e39ef7-a88b-577a-b0d6-705ea2d526fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474540} {:answer/id #uuid "87a04c93-3149-5e28-8454-384821f8c32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87a04c93-3149-5e28-8454-384821f8c32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474541} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2fed408-cdcd-55a9-a9f4-12abd80bada2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e26f992c-0caf-597a-b322-2e782bc69db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474542} {:answer/id #uuid "88843fa6-1855-53ff-af9a-14a6b6a49357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88843fa6-1855-53ff-af9a-14a6b6a49357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474543} :answer-field/id #uuid "2accb876-bb81-5087-87aa-41721160c992" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28567992-ba7f-5623-ad07-13abe4be416c" :question/math-academy-id "q-172325" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x+1>4$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $|x|>3$\n- **II.** $x>3$\n- **III.** $x>4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >4 \\\\ x & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|x|>3)\\,⇏\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then we have $x+1=-3≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>3)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>3,$ then $x+1>4.$\n\n- Condition III is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>4)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>4,$ then  $x+1>5>4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fd7e43-5c76-592b-aee4-f521964cb28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474690} {:answer/id #uuid "56db8c6a-3927-5f57-8d4a-f66704069758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22fd7e43-5c76-592b-aee4-f521964cb28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474690} :answer-field/id #uuid "5591e25a-3ea8-5f89-9be5-e954600bbcf0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475271} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aaacbae-01bd-5b78-b909-ba34f4a8bfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474692} {:answer/id #uuid "9df9fb08-bffb-50d9-9054-b845a6a759d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aaacbae-01bd-5b78-b909-ba34f4a8bfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474692} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3b5576e-92d4-5f62-a180-abf1cc0efd81" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a32688b-9a6e-5531-97e4-13b963ffda66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474694} {:answer/id #uuid "65d2bf31-d717-50e7-9174-4e253ccf20e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d2bf31-d717-50e7-9174-4e253ccf20e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474695} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd972e0-15e5-5c38-b69b-4c566a479a6a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "390cc44c-87e5-5905-81de-8b4495a342fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-216459" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $f$ is a differentiable function\n- **II.** $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$\n- **III.** $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇍\\,(f\\text{ is a differentiable function})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is a differentiable function but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne {sec}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1,$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne \\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$\n\n- Condition III is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a89bb0c-0c7b-56f1-b539-37a12390f125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474520} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae93c4e-dbee-5e05-a6c8-d9c42170ca16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ae93c4e-dbee-5e05-a6c8-d9c42170ca16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474521} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead4a86f-a7fe-5af4-9eb4-5b3a0b8b20db" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e692d5a-6355-5a16-ad53-70eaf6632af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474522} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f1e8fb-2da6-5ee5-9d4d-1da86e369e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e692d5a-6355-5a16-ad53-70eaf6632af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474522} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94fd077-0724-53df-91f5-264867194b12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6518693-7320-54ee-9d17-34a1c0cb7d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474524} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f11120-7136-5045-b049-91d280b83ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6518693-7320-54ee-9d17-34a1c0cb7d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474524} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd17e2ae-aab3-52ac-be51-99890d5d4e21" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b376045-26da-55cb-becc-db924f8d2dac" :question/math-academy-id "q-172302" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an odd number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n$ is odd\n- **II.** $n$ is a multiple of $3$\n- **III.** $n$ is a multiple of $5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,(\\text{ }n\\text{ is odd})\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is odd, it must also be true that $n$ is odd.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }3)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=7$ is not a multiple of $3,$ but ${n}^{2}=49$ is an odd number.\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }5)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=9$ is not a multiple of $5,$ but ${n}^{2}=81$ is an odd number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca89b64b-5016-52db-ad10-13fc71298748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453656} {:answer/id #uuid "bf064bf2-82e9-5e43-b653-633779214409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca89b64b-5016-52db-ad10-13fc71298748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453656} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a87b594-92ce-5651-a817-9591309b3dd4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field