pe {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede4ce41-af05-502d-be2d-e518a8a6f456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453662} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a732aa4-8287-58c7-a11f-321a281488be" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5116bec0-cc13-5aa6-83e8-d90bc6884457" :question/math-academy-id "q-183415" :question/problem "$\\,$ $(m>0\\,∧n>0)⇒(m\\cdot n>0)$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the true implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $m>0\\,∧n>0$ is a **necessary** condition for $m\\cdot n>0$\n- **II.** $m>0\\,∧n>0$ is a **sufficient** condition for $m\\cdot n>0$\n- **III.** $m\\cdot n>0$ is a **necessary** condition for $m>0\\,∧n>0$\n- **IV.** $m\\cdot n>0$ is a **sufficient** condition for $m>0\\,∧n>0$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,m>0\\,∧n>0\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,m\\cdot n>0\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $m>0\\,∧n>0$ is a **sufficient** condition for $m\\cdot n>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. $m\\cdot n>0$ is a **necessary** condition for $m>0\\,∧n>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "275eb9b3-6e5b-5c62-98b4-03f5eb30ad04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474684} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1d7d46-08e9-5f82-8332-0c08cdf016f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "275eb9b3-6e5b-5c62-98b4-03f5eb30ad04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474684} :answer-field/id #uuid "43cd0fdc-7d67-5615-af44-f39feac6c9d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f543881f-8b99-5c13-b785-3641b1d5fb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474686} {:answer/id #uuid "2882d536-f3b4-518b-b85a-785eed089933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2882d536-f3b4-518b-b85a-785eed089933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb42275-1db2-5292-815e-e65c000092bf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5589a6d5-b7d4-5595-bff4-bffeea5bfecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474688} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee035f5-77ee-597c-89c2-301f34f633df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5589a6d5-b7d4-5595-bff4-bffeea5bfecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474688} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4b9e5b-d610-515d-8a2a-ae5777bcd975" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5904ff03-6479-54c0-a38b-31e73684000e" :question/math-academy-id "q-216449" :question/problem "$\\,$ $12∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- **II.** $3∣x$ and $4∣x$\n- **III.** $3∣x$ and $8∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $2$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $12.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $12$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $3$ and $4.$\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇔\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇏\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }8∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=12$ is divisible by $12$ but not divisible by $8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee9453d-074a-5107-bbb4-b0abf0cb1738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453640} {:answer/id #uuid "522af7ae-7610-5307-bc48-8ff762788e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ee9453d-074a-5107-bbb4-b0abf0cb1738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453640} :answer-field/id #uuid "da8ef52f-8644-50f9-a33f-a8a2aaba5c4e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335ed2a0-6a3c-51b9-8485-9b4e39ee6c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453642} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c0daf7-8c21-5b80-8349-3f1e6870ee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5c0daf7-8c21-5b80-8349-3f1e6870ee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453643} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2395068-f8ab-5c71-97bb-67c230f86f39" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f09ba448-55d9-5d3a-8bc1-5dde7a2b15d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453644} {:answer/id #uuid "effca90a-310f-559b-9cd6-1949cd3b4c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "effca90a-310f-559b-9cd6-1949cd3b4c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d280a24-a16d-5b3b-963f-bb375f7da8e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} {:answer/id #uuid "e960af39-d3a3-5f17-8c2f-2ad92f587599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf101830-7404-5e46-b7dd-1e4d16a0cbf7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bbf3a4e-b9b9-5f74-9d97-2501c2b02398" :question/math-academy-id "q-183393" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $l$ and $m$ are coplanar and perpendicular lines, then $l\\cap m\\ne ∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **necessary** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n- **II.** $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines\n- **III.** $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n- **IV.** $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,l,m\\text{ are coplanar and perpendicular lines}\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,l\\cap m\\ne ∅\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines\n\n- Statement III is true. $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} {:answer/id #uuid "99a25cfb-7af1-584e-a23f-07d1873c1ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} :answer-field/id #uuid "16abb1e1-f335-5e47-9697-b110c37be556" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf8abdb-a012-5e69-b701-8cd5c59400ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474510} {:answer/id #uuid "00e746e6-7edf-5a02-bac0-109198a72497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e746e6-7edf-5a02-bac0-109198a72497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474511} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5cd708-41b4-5971-b4bb-2aec404fccd4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73900034-e9c8-5e7c-87af-8e3c53f25b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474512} {:answer/id #uuid "1149f043-cd71-50ca-9599-b2751718dde1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73900034-e9c8-5e7c-87af-8e3c53f25b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474512} :answer-field/id #uuid "471b8d11-4b50-5b5b-ba37-b436e873213e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ef2cacc-c405-55b2-8430-66b58129ad71" :question/math-academy-id "q-172298" :question/problem "$\\,$ $|x-2|=6$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $x>4$\n- **II.** $|x|<10$\n- **III.** $x=8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-2| & =6 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =-4,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of $|x-2|=6$ satisfies $|x|<10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x=8)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x\\ne 8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2f333be-b379-55db-a2cb-5b230d6296ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474574} {:answer/id #uuid "a5279a66-07ec-57a7-bb9e-535e8ba78ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2f333be-b379-55db-a2cb-5b230d6296ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474574} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f4abd5-a94c-52bf-9770-c5e45fbe660c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f67d93-7ed5-5d39-8f29-efe5dd8fbcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474576} {:answer/id #uuid "cec0961f-126b-58ac-a00e-2aecea8918ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cec0961f-126b-58ac-a00e-2aecea8918ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474577} :answer-field/id #uuid "7540f77e-125b-5cdf-a8c9-e205ca0e22bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475214} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b77f3b1-66c6-54d7-b4cf-6918eacddddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474578} {:answer/id #uuid "8298e019-7f7f-55ad-bd6d-8f876ec7a351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b77f3b1-66c6-54d7-b4cf-6918eacddddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474578} :answer-field/id #uuid "94175714-0186-5f94-b2de-ff35a6a19b00" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e1662ac-5299-5cc7-92ca-68567f121fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-183429" :question/problem "$\\,$ $20∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $10∣x$\n- **II.** $4∣x$ and $5∣x$\n- **III.** $100∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }10∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=10$ is divisible by $2$ and by $10$ but not divisible by $20.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $20$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $4$ and $5.$\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇔\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇏\\,(100∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=20$ is divisible by $20$ but not divisible by $100.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb05016-ebc2-5387-8920-8f619655786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474588} {:answer/id #uuid "48b8b3ed-0f8f-5b6d-8216-a969149d45a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb05016-ebc2-5387-8920-8f619655786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474588} :answer-field/id #uuid "5929b0d4-9f53-5302-b541-d4a631026b05" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320e0268-bb47-5058-9d07-2b67422add47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474590} {:answer/id #uuid "f7571c42-2ed9-58a2-ac68-52195ba3461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7571c42-2ed9-58a2-ac68-52195ba3461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474591} :answer-field/id #uuid "df033f1c-530a-5163-8431-c2cdfe6cba01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc295db-adb7-5a03-aa88-578d033a6fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474592} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc133e0-ab07-5ef0-aa15-ee3ec0ef27d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc295db-adb7-5a03-aa88-578d033a6fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e2035c-abbc-53ab-9142-02378bf8a91d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9dd0c0c2-7652-5690-ae78-53d067f574fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-183485" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(x)=2$\n- **II.** $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R$\n- **III.** $f(x)={x}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int 2x\\,dx \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nMoreover, the differential equation ${f}^{″}(x)=2$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\int 2\\,dx \\\\  & =2x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D\\in R$ is another arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇍\\,({f}^{″}(x)=2)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+x,$ we have ${f}^{′}(x)=2x+1,$ and so the statement ${f}^{″}(x)=2$  is true but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 2x.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)={x}^{2})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+1$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne {x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd4e79bf-48f6-5054-8a92-7d22fd13b6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453774} {:answer/id #uuid "55c2d1eb-0dac-55a2-baca-6bb8e8152c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd4e79bf-48f6-5054-8a92-7d22fd13b6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453774} :answer-field/id #uuid "28fead55-7c6e-562d-94d9-49bb978dd0c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b062392d-ea3d-5d3a-a2ee-f4f2fd2bd312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453776} {:answer/id #uuid "ab89074b-fa87-5c72-976a-23f02b7d6839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab89074b-fa87-5c72-976a-23f02b7d6839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453777} :answer-field/id #uuid "7db1f26a-d263-5899-8517-00aaebc4f4d6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a6e77d-803e-50d5-913b-e8c699094fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453778} {:answer/id #uuid "6533e143-1e66-57a7-b414-33d737dcadea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6533e143-1e66-57a7-b414-33d737dcadea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453779} :answer-field/id #uuid "7101900e-e89d-579e-87c9-b0fd8e65b140" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e23be71e-852a-5940-b70b-94df86be631d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453780} {:answer/id #uuid "b9562326-6917-5b9b-8891-e69c852ad350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e23be71e-852a-5940-b70b-94df86be631d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453780} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c87eaa8-597e-5f60-bf52-0bb03b1cc589" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd31a8b1-49f0-5bbe-9bfb-4daa99eb8e90" :question/math-academy-id "q-216328" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $P$ and $Q$ are congruent triangles, then $P$ and $Q$ have the same area.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area\n- **II.** $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles\n- **III.** $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area\n- **IV.** $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ are congruent triangles}\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ have the same area}\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles.\n\n- Statement III is true. $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "408df0cb-6c6f-5d9b-90f1-7f582171bc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474532} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c3c23c-90bd-53c4-815e-4acbcce6f3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8c3c23c-90bd-53c4-815e-4acbcce6f3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474533} :answer-field/id #uuid "c650a4e4-46df-5663-8cc8-623efe286c07" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9112523-8587-5ffa-8287-6ac21dbb9e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474534} {:answer/id #uuid "d42bf337-0cdd-5dad-902c-9e538740fc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42bf337-0cdd-5dad-902c-9e538740fc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474535} :answer-field/id #uuid "03bb3ee9-bab8-5ebf-9f70-e330a2b233ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ba5bf5-e61c-5fb1-91c6-c2c59dbcaad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474536} {:answer/id #uuid "fa034870-2511-553a-a643-bf518efcae8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ba5bf5-e61c-5fb1-91c6-c2c59dbcaad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d785b52-fdd9-556d-a378-0f57be058f85" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4cdd56d-10e6-5abf-be98-585e1ce87428" :question/math-academy-id "q-172322" :question/problem "$\\,$ $a\\ge 10$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $a=10$\n- **II.** $a>15$\n- **III.** $a>5$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a=10)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a=10,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>15)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a>15,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>5)\\,⇏\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $a=7,$ then we have $a≱10.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ebae4c6-911d-5b7a-81a5-489639363761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474666} {:answer/id #uuid "37584277-dd5a-53f8-ab90-99bca0e04e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ebae4c6-911d-5b7a-81a5-489639363761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474666} :answer-field/id #uuid "27021643-f42e-5623-ae73-432d54977b4f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902a3cbf-5052-5b08-8b8e-6c65dbb7c4b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474668} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4980a6-395d-529f-a3bc-ec28c85a6476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed4980a6-395d-529f-a3bc-ec28c85a6476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474669} :answer-field/id #uuid "916ce97d-4d5e-523b-92f1-ff944d43f48b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739985f7-aa1a-505d-8792-e69101c7b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474670} {:answer/id #uuid "c76a103a-9ee1-57f6-8fb2-89f461de2bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739985f7-aa1a-505d-8792-e69101c7b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474670} :answer-field/id #uuid "207c9ae9-3188-5600-be34-4699d2e652f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed1378b7-d665-5e7d-b9bb-42ac28cb1db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-216436" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0$\n- **II.** $x\\le 2$\n- **III.** $x\\ge 0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given inequality is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-2) & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x({x}^{2}+x-6)=6≰0.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,(x\\le 2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEvery solution of ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$ satisfies $x\\le 2.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x\\ge 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x≱0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9221a1-9cab-59c0-bf56-6f848a7e0e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474678} {:answer/id #uuid "c3cf31c3-f73e-5d77-b53d-a8d455c7cff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3cf31c3-f73e-5d77-b53d-a8d455c7cff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474679} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c70687e-b308-5f84-8a15-0e5dd9994cdb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a52e76-808e-5123-a481-05236f391726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474680} {:answer/id #uuid "0dcf35a2-41a1-5a2a-9a10-98ec347c21fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12a52e76-808e-5123-a481-05236f391726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474680} :answer-field/id #uuid "5089e15d-deca-5a6e-aece-72b0f44cadea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6b07157-b267-5eaa-9880-368af70fa7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474682} {:answer/id #uuid "73ad770f-d82f-590b-919c-e6168b3b87ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6b07157-b267-5eaa-9880-368af70fa7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474682} :answer-field/id #uuid "d95c6284-4027-528a-ae0b-3b8935544bfd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f653d451-6beb-59b1-affd-6d539e9553ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-216447" :question/problem "$\\,$ $18∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $9∣x$\n- **II.** $3∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- **III.** $72∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $18$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $2$ and $9.$\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇔\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇍\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $3$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $18.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇏\\,(72∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=18$ is divisible by $18$ but not divisible by $72.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048577 :topic/id #uuid "aae1aef6-2b7b-5139-9696-8862a8c42ce4" :topic/math-academy-id 2793 :topic/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "249e2dff-033f-5340-b2d2-ea5b106a947b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453648} {:answer/id #uuid "7124ea30-3bdc-5464-9843-2ce2517fcf9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7124ea30-3bdc-5464-9843-2ce2517fcf9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453649} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e121bcb-38e6-562e-95cd-1415caa73a9f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2226ea6e-d08d-51c2-b5c8-9e62a19f7a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453650} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf5bfdb-49fb-5a81-8e16-3fd1354ee488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2226ea6e-d08d-51c2-b5c8-9e62a19f7a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453650} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4bf9fb8-807e-5092-a71b-f5bbc71e0a25" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f1359a9-e2b2-535c-b05b-25bfab690331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453652} {:answer/id #uuid "1bdd2694-6ff8-5c86-9d82-3c8372d6a48f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f1359a9-e2b2-535c-b05b-25bfab690331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453652} :answer-field/id #uuid "142c805d-e505-5385-a031-31ee4017ce5c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a729f994-14c9-52ba-bb3e-944dfe6019ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453654} {:answer/id #uuid "195487bd-bfd6-5cbd-b556-5442da419935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195487bd-bfd6-5cbd-b556-5442da419935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453655} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d74078e-403c-53bb-b600-78b7e20a550f" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9b0e1b-3e64-5482-b003-6352af7b5cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-183396" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $A⊂B,$ then $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **II.** $A⊂B$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$\n- **III.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **IV.** $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,A⊂B\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement I is true. $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048376 :topic/id #uuid "9a5670e8-43ef-54b7-8f4b-81842fc55f1c" :topic/math-academy-id 3715 :topic/title "Flux in Two-Dimensional Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1e6a479-52d1-5ae4-939a-e3b5d03fd778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474284} {:answer/id #uuid "4890dcc8-ff49-5248-a3fb-0fe1da9aeb4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e6a479-52d1-5ae4-939a-e3b5d03fd778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f527906f-2d30-55d6-998b-e4e8bf90fc09" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb84b4f7-0bc5-5c5a-9056-122bbc70bc57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474286} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9a6aa9-acc4-5992-a14e-804d5a9c01a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb84b4f7-0bc5-5c5a-9056-122bbc70bc57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474286} :answer-field/id #uuid "65cb578f-78b5-5225-966a-db5a469b668e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fac217d6-6ce8-5003-9d34-2c9ea1c6c89d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474288} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc8acfa-931e-5f66-bebf-19feca6c0ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcc8acfa-931e-5f66-bebf-19feca6c0ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474289} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d35692f-6bb0-56b8-9a68-82c51fb3c32c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ae03bac-e2a8-5c3b-a5da-8c8f23590a03" :question/math-academy-id "q-127026" :question/problem "![](images/28/28a7eb32cfcd800c907e9f4af927eca7bd8616d36162682413db62a9feabefbb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *out* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/fe/fecf59674259d41222ffd981b1ab6d90c474fe2b0e37a6d5f7626f34536a6896.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/56/56a7fc09ed2a2a15b0949fa6041dc9c0ee6beb69f30b1a5c048afd8c57887d52.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048376 :topic/id #uuid "9a5670e8-43ef-54b7-8f4b-81842fc55f1c" :topic/math-academy-id 3715 :topic/title "Flux in Two-Dimensional Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2126782-b8eb-539b-8a44-4b656f8cdc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474278} {:answer/id #uuid "bc560dd6-7ac6-5a76-9df4-70c53f25e56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2126782-b8eb-539b-8a44-4b656f8cdc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474278} :answer-field/id #uuid "94621230-a9f0-50e7-b575-e0567a8c5e06" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e5a016-6e60-5487-bdda-a02e34603edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474280} {:answer/id #uuid "52b18bb0-cfb3-5c9f-948f-ea3749f36b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b18bb0-cfb3-5c9f-948f-ea3749f36b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474281} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d370b0-1e92-5c62-966f-578bba64458f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137d1b3d-a1ad-5c7d-a87f-d48c60a7cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474282} {:answer/id #uuid "6c50f32b-3afd-545c-a6cd-342f755fc462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137d1b3d-a1ad-5c7d-a87f-d48c60a7cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474282} :answer-field/id #uuid "3241e849-1133-58ff-a9e9-26f068ba66c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cc7cc51-6281-53f8-b74f-55c2a0b2fa6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127024" :question/problem "![](images/01/01d8d85064253b9241b1fd93c22381897f23556d6e02c5c2c0161c94cee3bbdf.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *in* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/bb/bb4fd4068760bb9132052b26508f0e1e0c02c45d425770de804b17ce7c512919.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is negative, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/46/46afd4cde01c95388c9daefbef0668ef696d5817ab9ea3614982edf58a9bdf55.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is negative, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048376 :topic/id #uuid "9a5670e8-43ef-54b7-8f4b-81842fc55f1c" :topic/math-academy-id 3715 :topic/title "Flux in Two-Dimensional Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86148950-3fc2-5f38-81ce-53ec93e76166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474290} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c0a1d4-d321-51db-9f9a-4313b742971e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86148950-3fc2-5f38-81ce-53ec93e76166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474290} :answer-field/id #uuid "eff65640-e27c-5010-a702-518eac2480f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa09f0c0-3016-5c6e-b7c4-55a245d9d0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474292} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c0e836-a991-5f1a-91a3-7effd835eb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c0e836-a991-5f1a-91a3-7effd835eb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474293} :answer-field/id #uuid "176d727d-d760-55bb-bfd3-626eda4dc691" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7817b13e-8e9a-530f-860c-d01aa3b29a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474294} {:answer/id #uuid "419f49db-2832-5c8c-8fb3-49f7638b7dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "419f49db-2832-5c8c-8fb3-49f7638b7dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474295} :answer-field/id #uuid "912976bb-a0fa-5d56-b533-8354e5ec824a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e18756f-1e50-5f09-be71-26f001c4f68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127027" :question/problem "![](images/af/afaec113101f1a63134d2b1cb5c9744b93f9b84dabafaa205780d2dc5b49a7bc.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *out* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/6b/6b24ece279cc480f20d7a4dbc65f7a5257af71f22688b1416c73e3b40673a321.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/9e/9e8527d26f0f2bd5372d8643f8f9321ec022bb0079e1fc5b23be4978f436613c.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048376 :topic/id #uuid "9a5670e8-43ef-54b7-8f4b-81842fc55f1c" :topic/math-academy-id 3715 :topic/title "Flux in Two-Dimensional Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc352a7-def2-5836-9338-8008f169268f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474296} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7131d4-fc3c-5f44-9a24-a7c8c38852ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d7131d4-fc3c-5f44-9a24-a7c8c38852ba" :answer/type {:db/id