ion.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "765f030b-c4cb-527c-8c26-c947b0ace6a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127028" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f1d25942ae680c068b587f38bfbc968c8850b8fa2db2003e994e1ec32dad892.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is negative\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Note that the flux $F$ that flows in through $C$ is the same that flows out through $C.$ Therefore, there is no net flow of $F$ through $C.$\n\n![](images/b7/b7acc3028de66ae71ae4e425da639e51a357a77f2b0a345290592cac91ba17d3.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/04/04639a0074aa4607fa57bfe589aad1780f8da6f573d8589a68c2fdb569b5a129.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "977dd536-4220-524b-931c-3ba60f55073d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474556} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbd00d-6155-5f97-ad98-53542fd4bb4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "977dd536-4220-524b-931c-3ba60f55073d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474556} :answer-field/id #uuid "251277cb-3ad8-5af9-897f-6f40b45fce72" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c59c1ac2-aac3-545b-8f90-1ae8a978cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474558} {:answer/id #uuid "741d8b65-925b-5a70-8aff-77354bc69797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c59c1ac2-aac3-545b-8f90-1ae8a978cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474558} :answer-field/id #uuid "d170f76e-4e31-5ac5-b1a2-1881ac8d197d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffc21ad4-56fc-56ad-8058-de8c73d359e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474560} {:answer/id #uuid "4843b0fb-74a8-5c2c-b516-cacac8678dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4843b0fb-74a8-5c2c-b516-cacac8678dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474561} :answer-field/id #uuid "254e65e2-d3aa-5440-89cf-3f8963043077" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c44203d-f0c3-504e-a004-3addf0955223" :question/math-academy-id "q-181956" :question/problem "If $A=\\{-2,2\\}$ and $B=\\{c,d\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times B?$\n\nI. $(-2,d,c)$\n\nII. $(-2,(c,d))$\n\nIII. $((2,d),c)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${-2,2}$ with ${c,d},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/98/98e7cfca515290b952ea5aefc9b2516a5cd6a68de0dc048c2075128e6c60b651.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(-2,c),(-2,d),(2,c),(2,d)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times B\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/1e/1e96aeb1c5bfb1f9faa590a8eb8b01528a1ce9431a3f1ceac92b156a9bdde221.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times B|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |B|=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((2,d),c)\\in (A\\times B)\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f010aa-4909-563a-a1c6-026ea372b9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453610} {:answer/id #uuid "cc594cdc-9b20-5045-955a-b97073ccd9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3f010aa-4909-563a-a1c6-026ea372b9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453610} :answer-field/id #uuid "17837e49-2464-5649-bf83-90cccc331115" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0283c69d-345c-50d3-b197-80ce0b36bc50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453612} {:answer/id #uuid "590b75d7-bead-582d-af00-04e682417e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "590b75d7-bead-582d-af00-04e682417e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453613} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96ebacd-74a3-5c9f-b150-1a708db2e23f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebbdbdd3-efff-5a4d-9fc3-2d71e2dbcfa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453614} {:answer/id #uuid "f355dabd-1bbd-5943-83a4-5e88ec291b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f355dabd-1bbd-5943-83a4-5e88ec291b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453615} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6c14f0-7877-5cdc-9923-b920790e1206" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f4365e0-4fb2-5b82-b78f-2c814bc881e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-182014" :question/problem "For the sets $A=\\{0,1,2\\},$ $B=\\{4,6,8\\},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(0,2)\\in C$\n\n- **II.** $(1,8)\\in C$\n\n- **III.** $(0,6)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/12/12d1b94cc6d53954a9c164bd069f77fcddc7a46de2c1701c1f4cdfc608eef185.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(0,4),(0,6),(0,8),(1,4),(1,6),(1,8),(2,4),(2,6),(2,8)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366 :topic/id #uuid "ef2fa709-af77-5fbb-a8d9-f92b628eeaba" :topic/math-academy-id 4422 :topic/title "Grammatical Constructions for Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177aca68-9ef3-57f2-8782-7922f7fdcee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474594} {:answer/id #uuid "27217023-5fb1-53d0-9a9b-49549b2e5ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27217023-5fb1-53d0-9a9b-49549b2e5ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474595} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e62a6b-b826-5d56-826c-3f7c9ec98dea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2dc5cc1-7434-55bb-a406-1d1e6e254658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474596} {:answer/id #uuid "05017e46-d244-50ca-8c96-927beaf7a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2dc5cc1-7434-55bb-a406-1d1e6e254658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474596} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d7d347b-6157-5d76-a456-77eb2150acb0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cce7b4dd-ecf5-5770-bb2b-64d8b861e198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474598} {:answer/id #uuid "f6556b17-607c-5539-b341-8b02d501a75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cce7b4dd-ecf5-5770-bb2b-64d8b861e198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474598} :answer-field/id #uuid "826f982e-2d81-59a1-b8ed-73e1e4460bd5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a88484f5-b344-5db6-b1d4-105554bbb0f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474600} {:answer/id #uuid "ff97cc03-e2de-5d2a-b9a5-83cfca9f550f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a88484f5-b344-5db6-b1d4-105554bbb0f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474600} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7c415d-face-5047-bf43-5a7f46334342" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-183510" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=-1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** $x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- **II.** $x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- **III.** For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$\n- **IV.** For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1,}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198282 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0809c075-e1be-5d49-b1fe-5433114bcf16" :knowledge-point/title "\"If-Then\", \"If\", \"Only If\", and \"Implies\"" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366 :topic/id #uuid "ef2fa709-af77-5fbb-a8d9-f92b628eeaba" :topic/math-academy-id 4422 :topic/title "Grammatical Constructions for Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0945ef13-941d-515b-b4ae-e682b2cbe6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474580} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b76547-30ba-5674-aaf4-f6a21243637d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0945ef13-941d-515b-b4ae-e682b2cbe6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474580} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb3d849-75e4-5708-89e8-c4fd195fa85d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b099b78-69e8-5b08-9c8f-7877b9604ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474582} {:answer/id #uuid "0570949e-7425-5fb0-95d5-a3cd6859565f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b099b78-69e8-5b08-9c8f-7877b9604ed9" :answer/t