ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e0b252f-632c-5fb4-955e-f2c2686886d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183448" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- **II.** If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- **III.** ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- **IV.** ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=4}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{implies}\\,\\underbrace{x=2}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{if}\\,\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=4}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,\\underbrace{x=2}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=4}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{only if}\\,\\underbrace{x=2}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=4}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{if}\\,\\underbrace{x=2}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\"" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366 :topic/id #uuid "ef2fa709-af77-5fbb-a8d9-f92b628eeaba" :topic/math-academy-id 4422 :topic/title "Grammatical Constructions for Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c97a67bd-0eab-522a-b912-f7d7b1965ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :