45499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474619} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b95fe8-12f9-57d5-b19a-d819c349b4a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50849cc0-0b42-5b52-abb5-e0bdf56880ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-183568" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $0\\le x<1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $|x|<1$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** Whenever $|x|<1,$ then $0\\le x<1$\n- **II.** $0\\le x<1$ whenever $|x|<1$\n- **III.** $|x|<1,$ provided that $0\\le x<1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,\\underbrace{|x|<1}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,\\underbrace{0\\le x<1}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{0\\le x<1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,\\underbrace{|x|<1}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{|x|<1\\text{,}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,\\underbrace{0\\le x<1}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\"" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049366 :topic/id #uuid "ef2fa709-af77-5fbb-a8d9-f92b628eeaba" :topic/math-academy-id 4422 :topic/title "Grammati