e381b-cb88-517b-9e8f-479328b7da2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453747} :answer-field/id #uuid "0424cae6-af37-5568-967e-b8349f54700c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee7950d-2e0f-561b-a855-dcda433c326e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453748} {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749} :answer-field/id #uuid "347ab12e-5830-50c8-b5fe-11a0cb0e2867" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b086cc6-e229-5377-bb89-5a8ff879bb27" :question/math-academy-id "q-214271" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $P(A),$ where $A={1,2,3,…,10}.$ \n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,|X|=|Y|\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(A),$ $|X|\\,=\\,|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $X,Y\\in P(A),$ if $|X|\\,=\\,|Y|,$ then $|Y|=|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(A),$ if $|X|=|Y|$ and $|Y|=|Z|,$ then $|X|=|Z|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049833 :topic/id #uuid "175206ba-6044-598d-974f-886a69e03c69" :topic/math-academy-id 2622 :topic/title "Equivalence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ca370f-8fd4-5122-9efc-7caeca9460d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd1bd756-3043-5134-837d-147e1313e4e1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c80d39e-eb35-5216-8249-21a7fefd55c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/