n A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${1}\\cap {1}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- Relation II is also not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${1}⊅{1}.$\n\n- Relation III is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049833 :topic/id #uuid "175206ba-6044-598d-974f-886a69e03c69" :topic/math-academy-id 2622 :topic/title "Equivalence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ce48c9f-99d9-5a57-a00b-4e4bf360757e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453758} {:answer/id #uuid "14605bc1-af90-5790-a615-0b1a9fadf2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14605bc1-af90-5790-a615-0b1a9fadf2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453759} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9fae93-f58a-52ee-974c-59c83db2d398" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454629} {:answer-field/c