-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "023c0a2a-6bf5-54dd-90e6-ef95b2cf26d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453765} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d24233-3893-5769-9223-4fd5ac58fcdf" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-214279" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={∗,⋆,∘,⋄}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄),(∗,⋆),(⋆,∗)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {∗,⋆,∘,⋄},$ if  $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$  then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(∗,⋆)\\in R$ and $(⋆,∗)\\in R,$ and also $(∗,∗)\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(⋆,∗)\\in R$ and $(∗,⋆)\\in R,$ and also $(⋆,⋆)\\in R$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Since $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, it is an equivalence relation.$\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049833 :topic/id #uuid "175206ba-6044-598d-974f-886a69e03c69" :topic/math-academy-id 2622 :topic/title "Equivalence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f596310-0e1c-53ef-9f1c-67543d48af1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474658} {:answer/id #uuid "d1bab53c-7396-5e9f-8554-262f35c8714b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f596310-0e1c-53ef-9f1c-67543d48af1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474658} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9bc8a91-e457-52a8-8f08-fda3fc0e439f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9273fd00-18f4-5b63-bc77-9c6f1bb11883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474660} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bd68a0-ec14-5260-8301-38a62f7933fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3bd68a0-ec14-5260-8301-38a62f7933fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474661} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6b08e0-fb69-544a-8ab