er/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453756} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c416ce7-be58-5360-a862-bf0f52fa3c15" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73719e8c-e17e-53b6-804a-0ade3bbbaa7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214273" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={a,b,c}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(a,a),(b,b),(c,c),(a,b),(b,a),(b,c),(c,b)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(a,a),\\,(b,b),\\,(c,c)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(a,b)\\in R$ and $(b,c)\\in R,$ but $(a,c)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id 