swer/id #uuid "f9f71df1-4716-5108-9e03-cef2e2d0d244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cef306a2-a1d6-50c7-8fae-5fc70f54757a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474648} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d6c947-e684-53b2-8702-320415a16119" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78aa39d2-6d95-5a7b-bd86-1b4658d3d903" :question/math-academy-id "q-214247" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $Q?$\n- **I.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$\n- **II.** $x=y$\n- **III.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy\\in N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${2}^{2}+{2}^{2}≰4.$\n\n- Relation II is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049833 :topic/id #uuid "175206ba-6044-598d-974f-886a69e03c69" :topic/math-academy-id 2622 :topic/title "Equivalence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90b7f96d-2c26-51b8-a503-b732dd7105e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474638} {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4680e212-67d2-5252-a922-ef475a60beba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} {:answer/id #uuid "39b3b2e0-da86-5014-bd8a-ee945f0ebf31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} :answer-field/id #uuid "1378d38d-6558-5839-92ba-4bd5499dd871" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} {:answer/id #uuid "b94689af-dc54-597e-8c18-94f6e4db05f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b62643e-bd65-5cdf-a6f5-99efc18252aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3f6ced1-e3e7-51b2-bdb3-c0561413aee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-214246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $N?$\n- **I.** $a\\,R\\,b$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$\n- **II.** $a∣b$\n- **III.** $a\\,R\\,b$ if $3∣(a+b)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is an equivalence relation. \n\n- It is reflexive because for all $a\\in N,$ we have that $a-a=0$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $a,b\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2,$ then $b-a$ is also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is transitive because for all $a,b,c\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$ and $b-c$ is a multiple of $2,$ then\n\n$$\na-c=(a-b)+(b-c)\n$$\n\nis also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- Relation II is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $3∣6$ but $6∤3.$\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $3∤(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049833 :topic/id #uuid "175206ba-6044-598d-974f-886a69e03c69" :topic/math-academy-id 2622 :topic/title "Equivalence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a285ab-48a9-5413-b7da-f2791d21aec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453766} {:answer/id #uuid "818ef40a-7f9f-549f-a73c-ef61315430d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "818ef40a-7f9f-549f-a73c-ef61315430d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453767} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6e6f971-d626-5e81-8ea9-2ca16e443ffb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454633} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "928474f9-40eb-5484-9372-fb4d6826d01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453768} {:answer/id #uuid "26e38cb8-cd99-500f-baef-1df11bb264c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "928474f9-40eb-5484-9372-fb4d6826d01b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453768} :answer-field/id #uuid "094e3f54-b5fa-5ceb-a1a9-f7bad7890846" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be8a9a8e-14d2-586e-b5d7-aa7bb9802705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453770} {:answer/id #uuid "7a48dbd3-9ebf-5e54-a131-4786a290165c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a48dbd3-9ebf-5e54-a131-4786a290165c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453771} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1cc8ff-5539-54e7-9a23-1eb634e86e6d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454635} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74744e0f-74ff-5c50-920e-156d87bec376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453772} {:answer/id #uuid "a52a0aaf-fd45-5ddc-b8ad-8881a84032fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74744e0f-74ff-5c50-920e-156d87bec376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453772} :answer-field/id #uuid "d347c014-5719-570c-9116-b736f2cfb1f8" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae54ed26-0094-5420-99d1-1b8455c5d0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-214280" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta }$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\alpha ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\beta )}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* symmetric because $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ but $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because it contains no \"linked\" pairs such that $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R.\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} {:answer/id #uuid "3e335ed9-b0c7-50b7-bf4b-dc3aedd3cf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e29da06-bfce-529c-931f-97c2357fe6fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad121aa6-d319-5297-af2a-e5e3093bb81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474564} {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b29ca3-f143-548a-ae89-a64c0ea33837" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd45a65d-0d13-5724-926d-fad0cc9c4e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474566} {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace444cf-7548-524c-92d8-dd3be4616e9d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd7d0702-ab54-5763-af3c-93c657eacc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181974" :question/problem "If $A=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $B=\\{x,y\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(B\\times B)\\times A?$\n\nI. $(x,y,1)$\n\nII. $((x,x),1)$\n\nIII. $((y,x),2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${x,y}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/5a/5af389ab817ce509519af7a3c1a5fdbb583d8e13859b9aa3b6166958f81e3040.png)\n\nHence, the set $B\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nB\\times B={(x,x),(x,y),(y,x),(y,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times B|=|B|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(B\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/da/dae7febad357be8d9f000c9dc7abfbe97fda34e3e9ff0b0e8ab0289e3c4e782a.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(B\\times B)\\times A|=|B\\times B|\\cdot |A|=4\\cdot 3=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $((x,x),1)$ and $((y,x),2)$ are in $(B\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049702 :topic/id #uuid "0cbdba81-6911-563b-9935-b7f4c99e46ed" :topic/math-academy-id 2642 :topic/title "Equivalence Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf894e-8578-5838-bb97-a01a04d5b043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e50a82-11c9-5ec6-83f0-10556f882d83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdc995a-9e19-5d0b-8013-21abcf455610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} :answer-field/id #uuid "817fe686-a8a8-5d25-a62f-e53303899546" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2df81f-2ec6-525a-a134-5bba469a3318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474874} {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875} :answer-field/id #uuid "d662e169-3539-5ca6-8143-0749449a329b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "071418af-96d7-52c9-8845-42c31b88cc12" :question/math-academy-id "q-77200" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{3}={y}^{3}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[8]?$\n\nI. $-2$\n\nII. $2$\n\nIII. $8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[8]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $8$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[8] & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x∼8} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,{x}^{3}={8}^{3}} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x=8} \\\\  & ={8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $8$ is in $[8],$ while $-2$ and $2$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049702 :topic/id #uuid "0cbdba81-6911-563b-9935-b7f4c99e46ed" :topic/math-academy-id 2642 :topic/title "Equivalence Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ffea43b-d86a-56b6-bcdb-ce67bcdc018f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604