d06fdfac-e110-5031-90bd-ef64919fe14d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78d51529-5603-5294-836c-698a99289cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-148394" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nI. The number obtained when picking an integer between $0$ and $10$ at random.\n\nII. The number obtained when picking a real number between $5$ and $9$ at random.\n\nIII. The number of clients arriving at a shopping mall in a day.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because there are a finite number of integers between $0$ and $10,$ and since the selection is random, each integer has an equal probability of being selected.\n\n- Random variable II cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because there are infinitely many real numbers between $5$ and $9,$ and so the support is not finite.\n\n- Random variable III cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the number of clients arriving at a shopping mall can be any positive integer, and each outcome is not equally likely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048884 :topic/id #uuid "c96d046b-16b8-5aad-81a5-2dd906b25702" :topic/math-academy-id 3269 :topic/title "Modeling With Discrete Uniform Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10973e79-c1b6-57b8-9851-6ae7106d412f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474996} {:answer/id #uuid "b6720f69-c55a-5a21-8a8c-910069c91507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6720f69-c55a-5a21-8a8c-910069c91507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474997} :answer-field/id #uuid "88439eea-1275-53b8-bdc6-f84f85c32054" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801b11e7-8369-5538-8992-5653a6bcbd70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474998} {:answer/id #uuid "60d00568-674e-59c8-a7b6-78f17e89c6b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "801b11e7-8369-5538-8992-5653a6bcbd70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474998} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd478cc0-8998-522b-b196-b9ffc3a11072" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5876226-3be8-5b2c-bc22-16b35fc71a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475000} {:answer/id #uuid "adf705a8-c994-5190-9fde-b08bcd7c7cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adf705a8-c994-5190-9fde-b08bcd7c7cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475001} :answer-field/id #uuid "939226be-c45e-56ae-9ecf-f6998f16c279" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc3edf0b-9469-5401-acc3-594a44dac66e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97753" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nI. The number obtained when picking a card from a set of cards numbered from $1$ to $12,$ at random.\n\nII. The number obtained when throwing a standard die that is biased toward landing on $1.$\n\nIII. The color obtained when a ball from a bag containing $5$ balls with distinct colors is chosen randomly.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. There are a finite number of cards, and since the selection is made at random, each card has an equal probability of being selected.\n\n- Random variable II cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. Since the die is not fair, each outcome is not equally likely, because there is a higher probability of getting $1.$\n\n- Random variable III can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because there are a finite number of distinct colors, and since the selection is made at random, each color has an equal probability of being picked.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c76b2b1b-7536-5b3c-a4c4-6f5e5b72e6ec" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Number by Zero" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049948 :topic/id #uuid "208ad900-2568-5e64-a594-cff48ca19048" :topic/math-academy-id 299 :topic/title "Multiplying and Dividing With Zero"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19dfb7ab-264f-5b26-bc13-11fda1da144d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474834} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6a2885-5ee5-54dd-a91e-78ddd4a1fcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19dfb7ab-264f-5b26-bc13-11fda1da144d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474834} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd2f74b-ad8f-5abb-91ee-9ca805b5a1e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde45ee0-4c6c-5fce-9f64-b97ee9a96a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474836} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a087e7-a5aa-51e3-8dd1-ca01571b6a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5a087e7-a5aa-51e3-8dd1-ca01571b6a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474837} :answer-field/id #uuid "b512f4fa-bc7f-5f53-a26e-9095140cf2c7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8d717e9-eb85-50d6-a373-90dc49898115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474838} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0b5d13-1db7-52ee-aeb1-3dfbc2fb2d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8d717e9-eb85-50d6-a373-90dc49898115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474838} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0d4d04-9d83-5a10-9980-4dbca36e9443" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3913baef-cd96-5f27-bb8b-fbabac946e82" :question/math-academy-id "q-43156" :question/problem "Which of the following is undefined?\n\nI. $0\\cdot 0$\n\nII. $\\frac{2}{0}$\n\nIII. $\\frac{0}{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We consider each point individually:\n\n- Multiplying any number by zero always gives zero. Therefore, $0\\cdot 0=0.$\n\n- We cannot divide any number by zero. Therefore, $\\frac{2}{0}=2÷0$ is undefined.\n\n- Zero divided by any number (other than zero) equals zero. Therefore, $\\frac{0}{-1}=0÷(-1)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046648} :activity/title "Mathematical Foundations I: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186