field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6266ee7-76af-56d5-9957-fa402398ddd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95923" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $8\\times 4$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is an $8\\times 4$ matrix\n\n- **II.** $R$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix\n\n- **III.** $R$ is an upper triangular matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $Q$ must be an $8\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. $R$ should be a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed $R$ must be an upper triangular matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050150 :topic/id #uuid "3185fbd2-cc78-5eb1-ba66-6a65b74ad8a2" :topic/math-academy-id 2547 :topic/title "Linear Independence of Solutions to Homogeneous ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9434ee35-97a1-5285-97bd-642508f58883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474768} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6